title: Add the parachain messaging pallet and route sibling XCM
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Penpal uses the new messaging pallet to send sibling XCM. To enable it in another runtime,
    configure the pallet as the parachain system's `ConsumptionRecordSource`, implement
    `SpecMsgApi` for collators, and use `EnqueueToXcmQueue` for the XCM lane. Run try-runtime
    before narrowing `SupportedVersions` or reducing `MaxMsgLen` for live channels.

    Place `SpecMsgRouter` before `XcmpQueue`. HRMP keeps priority until marked as closing.
    During cutover, new sends use the open spec-msg channel and fail if it closes. Drain both
    the sender and relay HRMP queues before requesting closure.

    Handle `AggregateMessageOrigin::SpecMsg(InChannelId)` in exhaustive matches on Cumulus and
    bridge-hub queue origins. Each inbound channel has its own queue and executes XCM with the
    sender's sibling origin. Configure `ChannelManagementOrigin` for cutover and queue control.

    For sibling XCM benchmarks, use the pallet as the `ToParachainDeliveryHelper` setup type,
    the router's `Price` as `PriceForDelivery`, and a destination with HRMP closed.
    Emulated chains can inspect block writes after pallet finalization through
    `AdditionalInherentCode::on_finalize_block`.
crates:
- name: cumulus-pallet-spec-messaging
  bump: minor
- name: cumulus-primitives-core
  bump: major
- name: cumulus-primitives-spec-messaging
  bump: minor
- name: cumulus-pallet-parachain-system
  bump: none
- name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
  bump: none
- name: frame-benchmarking-cli
  bump: none
- name: parachains-common
  bump: minor
- name: bridge-hub-common
  bump: major
- name: penpal-runtime
  bump: major
- name: xcm-emulator
  bump: minor
